{"tool_name":"dreamdia","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"dreamdia","home":"https://github.com/xmuyulab/DreamDIA-XMBD","license":"Apache-2.0","summary":"Software for data-independent acquisition (DIA) data analysis with deep representation features.","addition_date":"2022-05-12T19:41:37.212243Z","last_update_date":"2022-05-12T19:41:37.214987Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:dreamdia","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"jhan@xmu.edu.cn","name":"Jiahuai Han","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5592-4487","typeEntity":"Person"},{"email":"rsyu@xmu.edu.cn","name":"Rongshan Yu","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2179-173X","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Mingxuan Gao","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6619-6507"},{"name":"Wenxian Yang","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-5349-9680"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Deisotoping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3629"},{"term":"Peptide identification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3631"},{"term":"Quantification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3799"}]}],"name":"DreamDIA","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/S42003-021-02726-6","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021, The Author(s).We developed DreamDIAXMBD (denoted as DreamDIA), a software suite based on a deep representation model for data-independent acquisition (DIA) data analysis. DreamDIA adopts a data-driven strategy to capture comprehensive information from elution patterns of peptides in DIA data and achieves considerable improvements on both identification and quantification performance compared with other state-of-the-art methods such as OpenSWATH, Skyline and DIA-NN. Specifically, in contrast to existing methods which use only 6 to 10 selected fragment ions from spectral libraries, DreamDIA extracts additional features from hundreds of theoretical elution profiles originated from different ions of each precursor using a deep representation network. To achieve higher coverage of target peptides without sacrificing specificity, the extracted features are further processed by nonlinear discriminative models under the framework of positive-unlabeled learning with decoy peptides as affirmative negative controls. DreamDIA is publicly available at https://github.com/xmuyulab/DreamDIA-XMBD for high coverage and accuracy DIA data analysis.","authors":[{"name":"Chang Y."},{"name":"Gao M."},{"name":"Han J."},{"name":"He Q."},{"name":"Li C."},{"name":"Liu Y."},{"name":"Shuai J."},{"name":"Yang W."},{"name":"Yu R."},{"name":"Zhong C.-Q."}],"citationCount":1,"date":"2021-12-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Communications Biology","title":"Deep representation features from DreamDIAXMBD improve the analysis of data-independent acquisition proteomics"},"pmcid":"PMC8517002","pmid":"34650228"}],"topic":[{"term":"Informatics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0605"},{"term":"Proteomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0121"},{"term":"Proteomics experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3520"},{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0080"},{"term":"Small molecules","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0154"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"DreamDIA","home":"https://bio.tools/dreamdia","license":"Apache-2.0","summary":"Software for data-independent acquisition (DIA) data analysis with deep representation features.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:dreamdia/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":true,"registration":false},"packages":true,"source_packages":true,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"reposit